<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Romanians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Romanians are a people of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> who speak a Romance language derived from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>. Within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>, large Romanian communities lived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> and other eastern regions under Hungarian administration. Accounts of the Austro-Hungarian Empire list them among the many nationalities whose aspirations shaped the politics of the multinational monarchy.</p></div>
